{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EfCy4zeEmvH6fzzJHgoSLR","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t#!/usr/bin/env python3\n2\t\"\"\"\n3\thive — Autonomous agent orchestrator CLI.\n4\t\n5\tEntry point for running Hive agents against a labelled set of GitHub issues.\n6\t\n7\tUsage:\n8\t    hive run --project <label>              Execute agents on all open issues with <label>\n9\t    hive run --project <label> --repo o/r  Override the target repository\n10\t    hive deploy                             (not implemented)\n11\t    hive list                               (not implemented)\n12\t    hive remove                             (not implemented)\n13\t\n14\tRepository resolution order for `hive run`:\n15\t    1. --repo flag (per-invocation override)\n16\t    2. GITHUB_REPO environment variable (CI / Docker override)\n17\t    3. git remote get-url origin (auto-detected from the current repo)\n18\t\n19\tEnvironment variables (layered resolution — highest priority first):\n20\t    1. os.environ / shell exports  — always win; never overridden by any .env file.\n21\t    2. .env in cwd                 — per-project config (e.g. GITHUB_OWNER, GITHUB_REPO).\n22\t    3. ~/.hive/.env                — machine-level secret fallback (e.g. GITHUB_TOKEN,\n23\t                                     CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN).\n24\t\n25\t    The Docker / Compose consumer reads the repo-root .env via ``env_file`` and is\n26\t    unaffected by this layering — it does not call ``_load_env()``.\n27\t\"\"\"\n28\t\n29\timport argparse\n30\timport importlib.resources"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9ec0fa67-55b9-4089-8811-97bfd4c9a422","uuid":"6cab4c34-b0b7-49a1-a726-769030fe3d0f","timestamp":"2026-07-02T12:47:59.390Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/7z/4l2wtk591gq5dhp7bw5nh3fh0000gn/T/hive-cody-617j7amw/hive/cli.py","content":"#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"\nhive — Autonomous agent orchestrator CLI.\n\nEntry point for running Hive agents against a labelled set of GitHub issues.\n\nUsage:\n    hive run --project <label>              Execute agents on all open issues with <label>\n    hive run --project <label> --repo o/r  Override the target repository\n    hive deploy                             (not implemented)\n    hive list                               (not implemented)\n    hive remove                             (not implemented)\n\nRepository resolution order for `hive run`:\n    1. --repo flag (per-invocation override)\n    2. GITHUB_REPO environment variable (CI / Docker override)\n    3. git remote get-url origin (auto-detected from the current repo)\n\nEnvironment variables (layered resolution — highest priority first):\n    1. os.environ / shell exports  — always win; never overridden by any .env file.\n    2. .env in cwd                 — per-project config (e.g. GITHUB_OWNER, GITHUB_REPO).\n    3. ~/.hive/.env                — machine-level secret fallback (e.g. GITHUB_TOKEN,\n                                     CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN).\n\n    The Docker / Compose consumer reads the repo-root .env via ``env_file`` and is\n    unaffected by this layering — it does not call ``_load_env()``.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport argparse\nimport importlib.resources","numLines":30,"startLine":1,"totalLines":360}}}
